  "explicit_limitations": [
    "A/B/C rollouts are independent samples that can diverge before checkpoint interventions, providing run-level directional guidance rather than checkpoint-level causal effect estimates (§3.2, §F.1).",
    "Arm A executes unsegmented with a simpler prompt ('your only tool') and no check/probe middleware, whereas Arms B and C execute segmented with middleware; REFLECT relies on prompt instructions rather than a segmented-without-evolver baseline to discount this difference (Appendix H.3).",
    "DeepSeek-V4-Flash-0731 builds its own separate Meta-Skill rather than testing zero-shot transfer of GPT-5.6-Terra's Meta-Skill, and DeepSeek is not evaluated on DeepSWE 1.1 or against the five human harnesses (§4.2, Table 2).",
    "Offline precomputation cost ($110.19 TB Terra, $238.52 DeepSWE Terra, $81.90 TB DeepSeek) exceeds Continual Harness on single-evaluation full cost ($115.41 vs. $38.82 on DeepSeek TB; $174.91 vs. $112.23 on Terra TB), amortizing only across repeated downstream reuse (§4.3).",
    "Training batch count R, batch size, per-arm training rollout counts, and checkpoint wall-clock latency overhead are omitted from the manuscript; the cited project page https://meta-square.github.io/ had no indexed active repository in search.",
    "Evaluated benchmarks are limited to containerized CLI and single-repo code tasks with inspectable artifacts and automated verifiers (§F.1)."
  ],
